MiniOS Fluxbox package
=====================

Upstream baseline: Release-1_3_7, commit
88a74ff1cde22be3e894498ffd88934dc92dfef0.
The upstream version remains 1.3.7. debian/changelog owns the package revision.
The original MiniOS 1.3.7-1 quilt series is preserved; local changes belong in
additional Debian patches, not generated upstream files.

The Git tag does not contain the release tarball's generated manuals and
Autotools files. Prepare a build/source-package directory outside this checkout:

    ./debian/prepare-source /absolute/build/path/fluxbox-flux
    cd /absolute/build/path/fluxbox-flux
    dpkg-source -b .

The preparation command verifies the published original tarball's SHA-256.
No source or binary package artifacts should be written inside this repository.
Use the MiniOS build-minios-packages skill for development containers and final
clean Bionic amd64/i386 and Trixie amd64 builds. Debhelper compatibility is 11;
no runtime dependencies were added for the panel fix.

Tests
-----
The normal package build retains upstream make check and runs the standalone
head-geometry regression suite. To exercise actual X properties, window sizes,
fullscreen, invalid input, property deletion and panel replacement, run in a
clean build directory with an isolated X server (xvfb and xauth are test tools):

    xvfb-run -a -s '-screen 0 1280x800x24 -nolisten tcp' \
        debian/tests/check-struts ./fluxbox

Never run this synthetic-panel test against a user's desktop. The real MiniOS
session must also be checked with xfce4-panel, including resize and restart.

Desktop integration
-------------------
MiniOS's 04-flux-desktop skeleton owns the panel defaults and startup scripts.
Panels must publish their own struts: disable-struts=false on old Xfce panels,
enable-struts=true on new ones. The skeleton leaves these at the enabled default.
A package upgrade does not rewrite existing users' panel preferences or startup
scripts. Existing sessions need that preference enabled and the old fixed xprop
reservation removed. Fullscreen remains distinct from maximization.
